[rexglue-native] SDK 0308, released in setup tool 2.31.0 (2026-11-04; owner 04:35 "please start syncing
with release"). Native resolves at a draw resolution scale, color (Vulkan; on top of 0302; only with
native_render_targets on). New setting native_resolves_at_draw_scale (GPU, default off, applies at once).
Off, nothing changes; at a draw resolution scale of 1 nothing changes either.

With it on and a draw resolution scale above 1 (0014), a 32bpp 8888 color resolve without MSAA into a
scaled texture that already exists goes straight from the render target: one compute pass over the area's
host pixels (render_target_cache_native_scaled.cpp) writes each host pixel's word into the scaled resolve
buffer where the scaled resolve shader puts it (its layout and half-pixel gap fill), so the CPU readback,
aliases and textures made later get the EDRAM path's words, and shared memory gets the words the readback
takes, so the game's CPU reads see the same bytes as without it. The scaled texture is filled by an image
copy. Anything else takes the old path and logs the reason once.

Tested by rexglue-native-test on the owner's PC (2026-11-03/04), on the 2.26.0 release SDK with
0308 + 0309 + the async submit chain: at 2x and 3x (saint_lo, mp_merv, 4-player split screen at 2x) and
across live rescales; texture loads 0 MB a frame (xenos at 2x: 48.5 MB for one player, about 116 MB for
four), pictures within the run-to-run noise, VRAM unchanged, the Vulkan validation layer with sync
validation showing no new id (dev/agents/rexglue-native/R3-SCALE-ASYNC.md, R4-SCALE-TIMING.md,
R5-RELEASE-CANDIDATE.md; the draft's notes: DRAFTS-0308-0309.md).

